\details{
Stage 1 routes each retained cell type independently. At least two retained
conditions use the common-dictionary condition GRN; one retained condition uses
standard Pando. Pando parallelism is across broad-cell-type jobs and does not
create nested worker pools. Stage 2 reproduces the Stage 1 cell set and keeps
final metacells condition-pure. Stage 3 builds cell-type-scoped reaction
catalogues. Stage 4 produces the primary multiome reaction support and an
RNA-only control. Stage 5 defaults to original MATLAB CORDA2 on the complete
medium-constrained parent GEM for each cell-type-by-medium combination. CORDA2
keeps strict Step 1, Step 2.1, Step 2.2 and Step 3 barriers, parallelizes
independent directional targets within each step, reports completed and remaining
target counts, releases the stage-local pool and runs full garbage collection
before entering the next step. All public parallel stages share the same worker
budget and reserve two CPUs from the detected allocation. FASTCORE and full-GEM
remain supplementary routes. Stage 6 assembles rankings, annotations and
available condition contrasts. See \code{docs/tutorial-02-stepwise-audit.md}.
